window.docContents[102].resolve({"/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--Dimension-as-a-Forgetful-Functor--The-forgetful-map-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-19_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\nThe dimension map \nsends a kind-of-property to its PhysLib Dimension\n(ℚ-exponents over length/mass/time/charge/temperature). It is deliberately\nmany-to-one: that is what makes the dimension-1 disambiguation true.\n\nPlanned. Pulls in PhysLib + Mathlib as a separate library (the spine stays\nMathlib-free). Each base SI kind is assigned its unit dimension; derived kinds\nget the product/quotient of their factors' dimensions.\n\nDimensional coherence —  is a homomorphism. Whenever the interaction\nalgebra says  and  combine to , their dimensions combine the\nsame way:\n\nThis is the theorem that licenses forgetting to the dimension layer without\nlosing soundness: a kind-level product is always dimensionally consistent. Builds\non the dimension map and the kind product.\n\nPlanned. By the construction of KMul: a well-formed kind product is defined by\ncomposing the factors, and dim is defined to distribute over that composition,\nso the equation holds by rfl/unfolding plus Dimension's commutative-group\nlaws from PhysLib.\n\n","context":"PropertyKindCalculus Blueprint\u0009Dimension as a Forgetful Functor","header":"6.1. The forgetful map (Dybkær Ch. 19)","id":"/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--Dimension-as-a-Forgetful-Functor--The-forgetful-map-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-19_RPAR_"}});